    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 civic has been making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt? can u explain what that belt actually does and why a bad one would make that noise?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is responsible for driving critical engine accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor. A worn or slipping belt creates that high-pitched squeal because the friction pads fail to grip the pulleys tightly enough during acceleration, causing them to spin under load. If you are experiencing this, the belt likely needs immediate inspection or replacement to prevent damage to the engine components it powers.",
