      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Besides age and wear, a faulty tensioner or misaligned pulleys can prevent the belt from maintaining proper pressure, leading to slipping. It is also possible that the belt is glazed from overheating or has lost its internal fibers, even if it isn't obviously cracked. Most of the time, a combination of an aging belt and a worn-down tensioner spring is responsible for the loss of grip.",
